{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1010098-what-spheres-powers-would-a-priest-logically-use","id":1010098,"title":"What spheres/powers would a priest logically use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-30T01:00:13-08:00","id":1010098,"title":"What spheres/powers would a priest logically use?","content":"A member of the celestial chorus and or a priest, what spheres/powers would they logically have access to and use on a daily basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T02:06:55-08:00","id":1010114,"title":"","content":"It...highly depends on what they do, really. What are they doing?<br /> <br /> It is a preacher of sorts?<br /> Depending on how their, ahem, moral alignment is...Prime, to make people listening to them feel good and comforted (Being energized with prime feel quite vitalized), Mind to nudge their convictions, Spirit to seek Holy Inspiration.<br /> <br /> A worker at a homeless shelter, a wartorn country or an emergency aid establishment?<br /> Life to heal, Prime+Matter/Life and/or Entropy to make the supplies never quite run out when needed and bless people...<br /> <br /> A Crusader?<br /> Prime and more Prime for cleansing fire, warding off evil and protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T02:15:43-08:00","id":1010116,"title":"","content":"Depends on what type of Priest you are talking about. A warrior Paladin, a community priest that acts as the conscience of the community, a faith healer, a bible thumping racist? Are we talking about a Protestant , Catholic, Orthodox Christian or some other form of Christian Priest. Is it a Christian Priest?<br /> <br /> Priests are people with varying levels of conscience, ambition and empathy with lots of variation on skill sets, hobbies etc like the rest of us. <br /> <br /> What are their motivations, dreams, hopes etc?<br /> <br /> All of this will determine what kind of Spheres they have and utilise. As with all Mages in MtAsc, they have Access to all of the 9 Spheres. Question is how they use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:10:03-08:00","id":1010124,"title":"","content":"Let's go through this Sphere by Sphere. Much of this depends on what kind of Priest we're talking about.<ul><li>Correspondence: Being able to look in on one's church goers can be invaluable, as can the ability to find missing persons. (A local Priest has a duty to protect and heal their community, which may entail getting involved with such matters). An aid worker in a wartorn land could benefit greatly from the ability to move supplies and refugees over great distances. The base benefit of Correspondence could be used in conjunction with other Spheres, as a means of performing good deeds from a distance, as if by grace of God.</li> <li>Entropy: Sometimes a prayer for God's favor can make all the difference, so Priests may use Entropy to bless themselves or others. Entropy 3 could be used to make machines last longer before breaking down, which is helpful given how churches and charities rarely swim in equipment funds. Some Priests may elect to bring misfortune down on someone, as a means of pushing them towards more moral action (pain is a necessary evil at times, if it can teach the sufferer something). Disease and medical misfortune may be preempted with a few judicious blessings.</li> <li>Forces: Crusaders would obviously use this Sphere for its martial applications: fire, blinding light, force pushes, flight, etc. Even just making one's holy sword hit harder and one's bullets land true can be an invaluable edge. A Priest who eschews violence can still make use of Forces as a means of diffusing or avoiding conflict. Invisibility and Silence can be used to sneak undetected by enemies, and gravity can be manipulated to rob an attacker of their footing, so they have no choice but to hear out the Priest's peaceful overtures. Simple theatrical effects may employ Forces, working with sound, light, and warmth to sell religious experiences. Weather manipulation can bring merciful rain to drought-ravaged farmlands, and push harmful natural disasters away from populated areas.</li> <li>Life: An obvious Sphere for the miracle worker, allowing them to lay on hands and heal the sick. Subtle healers may ask the sick person to pray with them, using this act to weave a slow-acting healing that will play out over time (and thus be coincidental). Crusaders make great use of the ability to buff their bodies in battle, and to sap the strength of the enemies of goodness. Or to simply ravage the bodies of the wicked. Some holy warriors may elect to take animal war forms, usually related to noble beasts (lions, unicorns, etc.). More peaceful Priests may induce temporary paralysis in attackers, or draw them into sleep, so as to stop them without hurting them. Masters of Life may live for centuries - as it was written in the Bible was the case for early man - so that they may dispense wisdom for as long as the Lord permits.</li> <li>Matter: Combined with Prime, this can be used for the classic miracles of multiplication. Loaves and fishes, made in great abundance. The holy warriors of the Templar Knights have a variant that keeps their ammunition stores full during their crusades against evil. Matter could also be used to animate statues of angels, or to make the blades of enemies crumble in their hands, and their bullets' gunpowder turn to sand in their casings. A Priest's vestments may be made durable against wear, tear, and attack, not only lasting longer but giving Armor ratings above what's normally possible for their clothes. If nothing else, they can easily expel dirt and grime, keeping their outfits pure and clean.</li> <li>Mind: The Cabal of Pure Thought was so named for their mastery of their own minds, and any Priest could benefit from same. They know how their minds work, and can therefore spot the many deficiencies in their psychology that would otherwise cause them to sin. A Priest who knows the feelings (and thoughts) of others can more easily help them resolve their problems. Simple Mind arts may be used to prod people towards righteous action, and remind them of their better nature. Fiery passions can be soothed, and apathy dispelled, allowing the Priest to better resolve conflicts peaceably. A Crusader, on the other hand, may inspire courage in her allies, or terror in her enemies. Both the peace-maker and the crusader can benefit from the ability to strike the fear of God into their enemies. One Priest may emulate A Christmas Carol, and shape someone's dreams (along with Correspondence and Time) to reflect earlier events, as a means of teaching them lessons (this has the added benefit of being coincidental). Astral Projection, finally, can be employed to better commune with the heavenly host on its own territory.</li> <li>Prime: A common Sphere among Choristers, Templers, and others, because of its ability to protect and destroy in equal measure. As well as for being receptive to the fundamental building blocks of creation. Quintessence may be collected and distributed where it is most needed, and a Priest would seek to do so where it could do the most good. Even elementary Prime may be used to martyr oneself by converting health levels to Quint, which appeals to sacrifice-minded miracle workers. Swords and fists can be made to deal aggravated damage, while objects and bodies can be blessed to soak same. New spots can be sanctified with great effort, creating new founts of holy (read Quintessential) power. Prime can also bless (enchant) objects into Wonders, creating holy water or sacred swords, and many other wondrous objects besides.</li> <li>Spirit: Communion with angels is a common use of this Sphere, as is helping the unquiet dead move on to their final reward. Exorcists, meanwhile use Spirit to combat Satan's forces directly, driving them from profaned spots and casting them out from possessed people. Some Mages may journey into the Invisible World, seeking out fabled locations like Prestor John's Country or the Celestial City. Others use Mastery of Spirit to attempt creation of glorious Horizon Realms, where religious awe and godly work are the only powers that hold sway.</li> <li>Time: Fortune telling is usually frowned upon, though a Priest may ask God for signs and portents if it were in His plan. Disasters may be averted or better weathered with preparation. Historically minded Priests may employ postcognition in their scholarly pursuits, seeking answers to old questions by peeling back the folds of time. If a member of the Priest's flock were the victim of crime, the culprits could be viewed in the act should the miracle worker investigate. Crusaders make great use of a precognitive understanding of their opponent's moves, as well as the ability to alter the flow of time around themselves and others. With great alacrity, the most overwhelming odds may be overcome. If an Adept of Time cannot put down a demon, it could be exiled outside of the normal timestream, preventing it from causing any more harm until a more permanent solution may be found.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}